    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "641283bf_81871662",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T21:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the contentious part (or at least the part I thought would encourage discussion, which it has).\n\nThat makes sense to me. Just checking -- can we store on all platforms?",
      "parentUuid": "b64b2c9b_0f91aad6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "49ec0b37f12039dc85ff0b57262e16a0f9ca24a0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0d5f8c0_86f11c87",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T18:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure about D3D, but in vulkan the color and resolve attachments each have their own load/store ops. So vulkan could store for sure. I think if the caller is passing in the resolve attachment (assuming it is generic and has a load/store op), we should assert the resolves store op is a Store.",
      "parentUuid": "641283bf_81871662",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "49ec0b37f12039dc85ff0b57262e16a0f9ca24a0",
